# LLM Server Configuration
# The llama-server URL (without trailing slash)
# Example: http://192.168.x.x:8080
LLAMA_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Optional: the interface llama-server binds to (service/start.sh / start.ps1).
# 0.0.0.0 (the launcher default) is required for other laptops on the network to
# reach it — llama-server's own default, 127.0.0.1, is loopback-only.
# LLAMA_SERVER_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Shield proxy URL — required by loadgen/run_comparison.sh, which now sends BOTH
# the defense-off and defense-on legs to this same Shield process (toggling
# POST /admin/shield-active between them) rather than sending "off" straight to
# LLAMA_SERVER_URL. Not read by the shield itself (it binds its own port via
# SHIELD_PORT below); this is where load generators send traffic.
# SHIELD_URL=http://192.168.x.x:9090

# Optional: port the Shield proxy listens on (defaults to 9090)
# SHIELD_PORT=9090

# Optional: SHIELD_ACTIVE=false makes the Shield a pure pass-through logger
# (Day-1 behavior in CLAUDE.md) instead of enforcing admission control. This is
# only the STARTUP value — loadgen/run_comparison.sh flips it at runtime via
# POST /admin/shield-active without restarting the process.
# SHIELD_ACTIVE=true

# REQUIRED to be kept in sync manually: must equal the -np/--parallel value
# service/start.sh (or start.ps1) actually passes to llama-server (launcher
# default is 4 as of 2026-09-09). The Shield has no way to read llama-server's
# real -np at runtime. If this drifts from the real value, slot reservation
# (Defense C, concurrency layer) silently over- or under-reserves — no error, it
# just stops doing what it's supposed to. Whoever changes NUM_PARALLEL in
# service/start.sh must update this too. See docs/MANUAL_CONFIG.md.
# TOTAL_LLAMA_SLOTS=4

# Optional: fraction of TOTAL_LLAMA_SLOTS reserved exclusively for legitimate-tier
# in-flight requests (default 0.5). WARNING: if TOTAL_LLAMA_SLOTS x this fraction
# rounds up to consume every slot (e.g. TOTAL_LLAMA_SLOTS=1), default-tier traffic
# gets 100% rejected by slot reservation alone, before the token budget ever runs
# — the Shield logs a warning at startup if this happens.
# LEGITIMATE_SLOT_FRACTION=0.5

# Optional: cost units charged for a request whose n_predict/max_tokens is missing
# or <=0 (llama.cpp's own "unbounded, generate until EOS/context limit" meaning).
# Should be close to your per-slot context budget so an unbounded-output request
# is billed at its real worst-case cost instead of a cheap flat guess.
# UNBOUNDED_OUTPUT_COST_ESTIMATE=2048

# Optional: Shield's HTTP client timeout (seconds) when forwarding to llama-server.
# Must be >= the slowest client-side timeout any loadgen profile uses (profile-d.js
# uses 120s) or the Shield may kill and report a proxy error on a request that
# would have succeeded given more time. See docs/MANUAL_CONFIG.md.
# FORWARD_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120

# Optional: Prometheus scrape endpoint (if monitoring llama-server metrics)
# PROMETHEUS_ENDPOINT=http://192.168.x.x:8080/metrics
